{
  "summary": "Analysis of Card04 implementation for bounded downloader with GitHub-pages fallback. The current architecture handles redirects via `OnConversionFinished` but lacks a formal fallback mechanism for primary URL failures (network, HTTP, timeout, bad content, or validation). Validator failure (signature mismatch) occurs in `SubscriptionValidatorImpl` after the downloader completes and the converter produces `FlatbufferData`. To support fallback without activating invalid data, the downloader must catch `ConversionResult` errors or empty data and trigger a secondary request to the mapped GitHub-pages URL, maintaining the original subscription identity and privileges. Boundedness is enforced via `kMaxNumberOfRedirects` and `AdblockResourceRequest::RetryPolicy`, but explicit payload size limits and timeout controls must be added to `AdblockResourceRequestImpl` to satisfy Card04 requirements.",
  "architecture_observations": [
    "Current redirect logic is embedded in `OnConversionFinished`, which is part of the conversion phase, not the transport phase.",
    "Validator failure happens post-download/post-conversion, meaning the file is already on disk.",
    "Identity (subscription_url) is used as the key in `ongoing_downloads_`, which must be preserved during fallback.",
    "The `AdblockResourceRequest` does not currently expose a way to set explicit payload size bounds or hard timeouts.",
    "Cancellation logic in `CancelDownload` correctly erases the entry, preventing stale callbacks from acting on the primary URL."
  ],
  "proposed_changes": [
    {
      "file": "components/adblock/core/subscription/subscription_downloader_impl.h",
      "change": "Add `std::map<GURL, GURL> fallback_urls_` to track approved GitHub-pages mappings. Add `void TriggerFallback(const GURL& primary_url)` to handle the transition."
    },
    {
      "file": "components/adblock/core/net/adblock_resource_request_impl.h",
      "change": "Add `void SetMaxPayloadSize(size_t bytes)` and `void SetTimeout(base::TimeDelta timeout)` to the interface and implementation."
    },
    {
      "file": "components/adblock/core/subscription/subscription_downloader_impl.cc",
      "change": "Modify `OnConversionFinished` to detect `ConversionError` or empty `FlatbufferData`. If a fallback exists for the current `subscription_url`, call `TriggerFallback` instead of `AbortWithWarning`. In `TriggerFallback`, initiate a new `StartDownload` using the fallback URL but preserving the original `subscription_url` as the identity for `persistent_metadata_` and `conversion_executor_`."
    }
  ],
  "patch": "",
  "risks": [
    "Fallback logic could lead to infinite loops if the fallback URL also fails and points back to the primary (though mapping is one-way).",
    "Preserving identity while changing transport URL must be carefully audited to ensure `persistent_metadata_` doesn't create duplicate entries for the same logical subscription."
  ],
  "tests": [
    "Unit test: Simulate `ConversionResult` error and verify `StartDownload` is called with the mapped GitHub-pages URL.",
    "Unit test: Verify that a validator failure (signature mismatch) triggers the fallback mechanism.",
    "Integration test: Ensure `kMaxNumberOfRedirects` is respected even when a fallback is triggered."
  ]
}
